      <meta name="description" its:translate="yes">Learn how to configure systemd-coredump, collect and analyze core dumps, and manage crash data and storage</meta>

      <abstract>
        <para><literal>systemd-coredump</literal> is a system service in &productname; that automatically collects, compresses, and logs application core dumps when processes crash. By capturing process memory images and storing them alongside &systemd; journal metadata, it enables administrators to easily inspect crash stack traces, manage storage retention policies, and debug application failures using utilities like <command>coredumpctl</command> and gdb.</para>
